        "Ismail requested his father to bind his ropes tightly and sharpen the knife so that his mother would not see his struggle. When both yielded their wills to the Almighty and Ibrahim pressed the blade to Ismail's neck, Allah halted the knife, declaring: ﴿وَنَادَيْنَاهُ أَن يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ * قَدْ صَدَّقْتَ الرُّؤْيَا إِنَّا كَذَٰلِكَ نَجْزِي الْمُحْسِنِينَ * إِنَّ هَٰذَا لَهُوَ الْبَلَاءُ الْمُبِينُ * وَفَدَيْنَاهُ بِذِبْحٍ عَظِيمٍ﴾ 'We called to him, \"O Abraham, you have fulfilled the vision!\" Indeed, We thus reward the doers of good... And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice.' (Surah As-Saffat 37:104-107). Ismail earned the eternal honor of 'Dhabihullah' (The Sacrificed of Allah).",
